  "limitations": [
    "Reviewed by a fresh read-only `codex exec` invoked by hand, not by `xtask review`: the controller's predecessor gate refuses P09 subjects until C26 completes; D058 and the owner's 2026-10-26 instruction authorise proceeding. Receipts are regenerated through the controller once C26 completes.",
    "The working tree holds the owner's uncommitted C26 attempt-02 and academy-2.1 work, excluded from scope; the input inventory covers the compiled and tested sources.",
    "`xtask check`/`xtask test` as whole commands were not run (they would include the owner's in-progress work); their constituent commands relevant to this chunk were run individually with exit codes and log hashes recorded.",
    "The chunk's work is committed on branch c41-api at HEAD (the pre-gate commit 70b4a920, the driver fix a12d20a8 and the first-native-run fixes 65f141f4: a save's word gives way to Unsaved changes on the next edit, the request tree stacks above the editor below 760px, the driver returns to the list request's tab before the keyboard send; and the second-run fixes: the status line's last word (a send's completion too) gives way to Unsaved changes on the next edit, the title row's chips shrink instead of widening the row at 200%; and the third-run fix: the view follows the core's tab selection only when it changes, so a snapshot from before + no longer re-opens the previous request over the new draft (the core then selected it again); and the attempt-01 remediation abc05a3b (docs/planning/reviews/C41/remediation-attempt-01.md): following the selection is scoped to the open collection, the request tree is a hierarchy with descendant counts, a tool sheet returns focus to the Collection chip through Modal's explicit returnFocus, every edit settles the status line, and native N01 asserts the keyboard open/close focus return. Attempt-02 scored 9/8/9/8/8 with no blockers and was accepted at 8 under D034 (reviews/C41/attempt-02/acceptance.md); its one failure is remediated in 5a5a1282 (reviews/C41/remediation-attempt-02.md): the Params and Headers rows are verbatim (a trailing space survives as it is typed, a padded query value stays padded when another row is edited, a header keeps its colon spacing), with a character-by-character multiword and padded-value regression asserting the exact Save and Send fields. Attempt-03 scored 9/8/9/8/8 with no blockers and was accepted at 8 under D034 (reviews/C41/attempt-03/acceptance.md); its one failure is remediated in da076440 (reviews/C41/remediation-attempt-03.md): the response pane's head always shows a transfer in flight with its Cancel request above whatever run is inspected, with a regression holding Send pending after showing an older run from History (Cancel dispatches the active run once, history as recorded, one send). Attempt-04 scored 9/8/9/8/8 with no blockers (reviews/C41/attempt-04/acceptance.md); its one failure is remediated in f1083fce (reviews/C41/remediation-attempt-04.md): every transfer in flight for the shown request is listed with its own Cancel request (named N of M when several), with a regression of two deferred sends across a tab round trip, each cancelled by its own id exactly once and nothing resent. Attempt-05 scored 9/8/9/8/8 with no blockers (reviews/C41/attempt-05/acceptance.md); its three failures are remediated in 3d1827bf (reviews/C41/remediation-attempt-05.md): only the latest load of the selected request counts and a document result shows only for the collection it was asked of (R1), a refused or undelivered load is shown in the editor's place with its reason and Try again, no automatic retry (R2), and a tool's failed action is said as an alert inside its sheet with entered work and focus kept (R3), each with a component regression. Attempt-06 scored 9/8/9/8/8 with no blockers (reviews/C41/attempt-06/acceptance.md); its three failures are remediated in 460778b1 (reviews/C41/remediation-attempt-06.md): every document reply is a load bound to its collection and generation, the tree's open and a new request's or cURL import's draft included, a load of another request is retired when the selection moves on (R1); a collection boundary retires the loading marker so a re-opened selection loads afresh while the previous lifetime's reply stays ignored (R2); a refused or undelivered creation is said inside the New request dialog with the path and focus kept (R3), each with a component regression. Attempt-07 scored 9/8/9/8/8 with no blockers (reviews/C41/attempt-07/acceptance.md); its two failures are remediated in 4db4508e (reviews/C41/remediation-attempt-07.md): a cURL import's load begins before dispatch and its reply settles against that collection and generation (R1), and a failed tree load names its request and is said above the current editor whatever the selection, with Try again and no automatic retry (R2), each with component regressions; BASE_REF=73048f76) in its own worktree branched from C40's commit 73048f76 (on c40-cases, itself from C39b's 49a5bac1, C39a's 640103e7 and main's C38 1ff6fe17), so the earlier chunks' gates stayed in scope; scope and diff.patch are measured from 73048f76. The owner's uncommitted build files (xtask sources, Cargo.lock, the Tauri manifests, the desktop-core version bump, the harness pin, the legacy feature views) are present as uncommitted copies, excluded from scope as the owner's work; the v2 API Client imports none of the legacy views (WorkbenchView and the legacy editor are not imported; the text helpers in workbench-call.ts are shared). Native acceptance C41-N01..N02 recorded against the rebuilt fixture bundle (native-prepare.json; executable hash bound in native-acceptance.json) with AX trees, self-captures and the measured layout matrix under evidence/C41/screens, against a plain-HTTP loopback service for the collection's requests. The owner's dependency amendment of 2026-10-30 applies (approved in the owner's words, \"Dependency amendment approved\"): P09 chunks are reviewed on their own worktrees from each predecessor's pre-gate commit; predecessor remediation is integrated by the merge chain and validated by the P09 phase review, so a chunk's review takes the predecessor's record as it stands.",
